# Architecture

Purpose: layer boundaries and dependency direction for HOSSPI HMS frontend.

## Style

Feature-first clean architecture:

```txt
presentation -> domain -> data contracts
              data implementation -> external services
```

## Mandatory rules

- Widgets must not call APIs, databases, secure storage, or sync services directly.
- Widgets must read display data only from Riverpod providers/controllers — no authoritative `setState` or local caches of server data (see [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc)).
- Widgets must not store tokens or secrets.
- Repositories must not show dialogs, snackbars, or navigate.
- Data sources must not contain UI state.
- Domain entities must not depend on Flutter widgets.
- `core` must not contain feature-specific business rules.
- Feature modules expose only intentional public entry points.
- Workspace controllers that show shared data must register realtime listeners (see [`realtime_sync.mdc`](./realtime_sync.mdc)).
- Use cases required when business decisions span multiple repositories or rules.
- Mapping between DTOs, database models, and domain entities must be explicit.

## Layer ownership

| Layer | Owns | Must not own |
|---|---|---|
| Presentation | pages, widgets, controllers, UI state | API, SQL, tokens |
| Domain | entities, contracts, use cases | JSON parsing, widgets |
| Data | repos, DTOs, mappers, data sources | navigation, UI messages |
| Core | cross-cutting infrastructure | feature business rules |
| Shared UI | reusable components/layouts | domain decisions |

